   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Mobile** (1 review): The reviewer singles out this performance of Mobile as a particular favorite [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Idylls of the King**: rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Mobile**: back after 56 archived shows (526 days); rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Doc Gooden**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **My Favorite Things**: back after 47 archived shows (447 days); rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Prana Ferox**: back after 40 archived shows (408 days) [3]\n- **Lion's Teeth**: back after 55 archived shows (524 days) [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2024-12-09** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 21 songs; 99 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Portland, duo transition + lead-in, thank god I'm a country boy! + no children [1]\n- The crowd reacted audibly to My Favorite Things and Waylon Jennings Live!, and sang the wordless BA BA BAAA part [2]\n- The band and Paper Tiger staff supported the taping of this show [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2024-12-09**: taped by astrolyric; transferred by astrolyric; source: Sony PCM-A10 (AUD) + SBD > Sony PCM-A10 [1]. Also: This is a matrix recording, the fourth matrix in a row from the same taper; Soundboard source, the uploader's first, made with help from tour manager and engineer Brandon Eggleston and venue sound person Coby [1][2]",
